d for which years. base_page &lt;- &quot;https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/gis/archive_besttrack.php?year=&quot; base_zip &lt;- &quot;https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/gis/best_track/&quot; hurricane_years_interest &lt;- 2008:2025 #getting data for all years from 2008 to 2025 Next, we set up the storage location for the hurricane best track files and create a lookup table for later. It is important to set a viable output directory for the best tracks from the website. #set an output directory for the data to download into base_shape_dir &lt;- &quot;./data/HurricaneRawData/nhc_best_tracks&quot; dir.create(base_shape_dir, showWarnings = FALSE) #create a lookup table for the storms that can be used later to create a connection between the storm name and data storm_summary &lt;- data.frame(Year = integer(), Storms = integer()) storm_lookup &lt;- data.frame(year = integer(), storm_id = character(), storm_name = character()) Finally, get the files from the website for each year specified. Within this snippet, a lookup table for the file names and actual hurricane name is created and saved as a .csv for later reference. (TODO: add a switch to get just the names list vs. the file and names list) #process every year for the year range specified above for (year in hurricane_years_interest) { cat(&quot;processing&quot;, year, &quot;
